ates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.54$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.54$ | $0.59$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/30/30d1e296e7c83fa8925feb116c9035de14790e89ddad37ab44710feacadf13a8.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ and ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{converges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/05/054b319170c634494c703d9588419cb6e44414196c970ca0c39689bc62f90d97.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334301" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =3\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49d51940-1d42-5a6c-821f-8629f9249cb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427138 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=3>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4de2f066-5f99-55ca-83ec-a830f6566d95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427139 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector